        </div>

       <div class="ch">
    <h1>3rd-Order Chebyshev Low-Pass Filter - PyAMS AC Analysis</h1>

    <div class="ch-card">
        <h2>Circuit Specifications</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Filter Type:</strong> 3rd-Order Chebyshev Type I (T-Network LC Ladder)</li>
            <li><strong>Cutoff Frequency (fc):</strong> 1000 Hz (1 kHz)</li>
            <li><strong>Passband Ripple:</strong> 0.5 dB</li>
            <li><strong>Characteristic Impedance (Z0):</strong> 100 Ω</li>
            <li><strong>Source Resistor (Rs):</strong> 100 Ω</li>
            <li><strong>Load Resistor (RL):</strong> 100 Ω</li>
            <li><strong>Inductor 1 (L1):</strong> 25.4 mH</li>
            <li><strong>Capacitor 1 (C1):</strong> 1.75 µF</li>
            <li><strong>Inductor 2 (L2):</strong> 25.4 mH</li>
            <li><strong>Input (V1):</strong> AC Voltage Source (1V amplitude)</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <h2>Chebyshev Polynomial &amp; Transfer Function</h2>
    <div class="ch-formula">
        |H(jω)|² = 1 / [1 + ε² · T²₃(ω/ωc)]<br>
        T₃(x) = 4x³ − 3x &nbsp;&nbsp;(for n = 3)<br>
        Ripple parameter: ε = √(10^(0.1·R_dB) − 1) = √(10^0.05 − 1) ≈ <strong>0.3493</strong>
    </div>

    <h2>Normalized Prototype Values (g-parameters)</h2>
    <div class="ch-formula">
        g₁ = 1.5963 (L1) → L1 = (g₁ · Z0) / (2πfc) = (1.5963 × 100) / 6283.185 ≈ <strong>25.4 mH</strong><br>
        g₂ = 1.0967 (C1) → C1 = g₂ / (2πfc · Z0) = 1.0967 / (6283.185 × 100) ≈ <strong>1.75 µF</strong><br>
        g₃ = 1.5963 (L2) → L2 = (g₃ · Z0) / (2πfc) = (1.5963 × 100) / 6283.185 ≈ <strong>25.4 mH</strong>
    </div>

    <h2>Simulation &amp; Response Characteristics</h2>
    <div class="ch-grid">
        <div class="ch-col blue">
            <h3>Magnitude Response (dB)</h3>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Passband (f &lt; 1 kHz):</strong> Equiripple behavior within 0.5 dB band</li>
                <li><strong>Insertion Loss:</strong> -6 dB baseline due to matched 100 Ω source and load termination</li>
                <li><strong>Cutoff (1 kHz):</strong> Reaches -6.5 dB (0.5 dB below peak)</li>
                <li><strong>Stopband Roll-off:</strong> Steep -60 dB/decade (-18 dB/octave) slope</li>
                <li><strong>Attenuation at 3 kHz:</strong> &gt; 32 dB attenuation</li>
                <li><strong>Attenuation at 10 kHz:</strong> &gt; 62 dB attenuation</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="ch-col red">
            <h3>Phase &amp; Group Delay</h3>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Low Frequency:</strong> Nearly linear phase near 0°</li>
                <li><strong>At Cutoff (1 kHz):</strong> Phase shift around -135°</li>
                <li><strong>Stopband (f &gt; 3 kHz):</strong> Phase approaches asymptotic transition</li>
                <li>Higher selectivity achieved compared to Butterworth of identical order</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="ch-card green-border">
        <h2>Conclusion &amp; Applications</h2>
        <p style="line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">Chebyshev Type I filters provide a significantly <strong>steeper transition</strong> between the passband and stopband than Butterworth or Bessel filters of the same order, at the expense of controlled ripple in the passband. This makes them ideal for RF front-ends, channel selection in communications systems, audio crossover networks, and anti-aliasing pre-filters where sharp out-of-band rejection is critical.</p>
    </div>
</div>
    </div>
    </div></foreignObject></g><g x="35" y="50" transform="translate(35,50)" width="35" height="55" class="part" name="part" xo="0" yo="0" sref="V1" directory="Source"><g width="180" height="100" zoom="16.399999999999974" left="226" top="266" symbol="{&quot;name&quot;: &quot;AC Voltage&quot;, &quot;reference&quot;: &quot;V&quot;, &quot;device&quot;: {&quot;type&quot;: &quot;SPICE&quot;, &quot;name&quot;: &quot;Voltage Source&quot;}, &quot;model&quot;: {&quot;name&quot;: &quot;ACVoltage&quot;, &quot;file&quot;: &quot;ACVoltage.py&quot;, &quot;dir&quot;: &quot;library&quot;, &quot;local&quot;: true, &quot;setParams&quot;: &quot;Vac=1V&quot;}, &quot;description&quot;: {&quot;webPage&quot;: &quot;&quot;, &quot;info&quot;: &quot;&quot;}}"></g><g points="20,5 20,15" class="polyline" name="pin" type="simple" netid="0" netidpos="2" netId="0" netIdPos="2"><polyline points="20,5 20,15 " style="stroke: rgb(255, 0, 0); stroke-width: 1px;"></polyline><rect width="6" height="6" class="pin" x="17" y="2" style="stroke: rgb(0, 255, 0); fill: none; stroke-width: 1px; display: none;"></rect><text r="0" x="18" y="17" transform="rotate(90 18 17)" style="font-size: 12px; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; display: none; fill: rgb(0, 0, 0);">p</text><text r="0" x="20" y="5" transform="rotate(0 20 5)" style="font-size: 12px; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; display: none;">+</text><ellipse cx="20" cy="13.5" rx="1.5" ry="1.5" style="stroke: rgb(255, 0, 0); fill: rgb(255, 0, 0); stroke-width: 1px; display: none;"></ellipse><polygon points="18.5,15 21.5,15 20,16.5 " style="stroke: rgb(255, 0, 0); fill: rgb(255, 0, 0); stroke-width: 1px; display: none;"></polygon></g><g points="20,55 20,45" class="polyline" name="pin" type="simple" netid="4" netidpos="0" netId="4" netIdPos="0"><polyline points="20,55 20,45 " style="stroke: rgb(255, 0, 0); stroke-width: 1px;"></polyline><rect width="6" height="6" class="pin" x="17" y="52" style="stroke: rgb(0, 255, 0); fill: none; stroke-width: 1